From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 11:37:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/haswell: Power the panel up at wake under macOS

With gfx_resume_init off, the S3 resume path leaves the panel with VDD
only, for its HPD, and the graphics driver of the OS powers it up. macOS
drives the panel of the W541, on DDI D, as a DisplayPort sink: at wake
it trains the link and runs the pipe, but it never powers the panel up
through the panel power sequencer nor enables the backlight, and the
display stays black. With the option on, libgfxinit does both
(PP_CONTROL 0x07), and macOS finds the panel lit.

Under macOS, power the panel up with its backlight from _WAK (3), after
the backlight level is put back: power on, power down on reset and
backlight enable in PP_CONTROL, at the BAR of the moment, as libgfxinit
sets them. Only from the state that the resume path leaves with the
option off, VDD forced on and nothing else: with the option on, the
panel is lit already. The forced VDD stays: macOS does not touch the
sequencer, and S3 clears it. Linux and Windows power the panel up
themselves, and i915 warns about a panel that it finds powered up.

An OpenCore table for the W541 (SSDT-PNLWAK, with the _WAK of the DSDT
renamed) does the same, and waits for the panel when HPD is low; the
resume path leaves HPD high before the OS runs, so _WAK does not wait.

TEST=Built lenovo/w541 with mrc.bin and with the native RAM init. In
acpiexec on its DSDT, with _OSI ("Darwin") answered, _WAK (3) turns a
PP_CONTROL of 0x8 at BAR0 + 0xc7204 into 0xf (0xabcd0008 into
0xabcd000f) and leaves 0, 0x2, 0x7 and 0xf as they are, _WAK (4) changes
nothing, and nothing is accessed without a BAR; without "Darwin" nothing
changes. The checks of the earlier ACPI patches give the same results.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/panel.asl   | 30 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../lenovo/haswell/acpi/platform.asl          | 11 +++++++
 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/dsdt.asl         |  2 ++
 3 files changed, 43 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/panel.asl

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/panel.asl b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/panel.asl
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..a05ec830f1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/panel.asl
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later */
+
+Scope (GFX0)
+{
+	/*
+	 * Power the panel up with its backlight, through the panel power
+	 * sequencer of the PCH (PP_CONTROL, at the BAR of the moment), as
+	 * libgfxinit does at wake with gfx_resume_init on: power on, power down
+	 * on reset, backlight enable. Only from the state that the resume path
+	 * leaves with the option off, VDD forced on and nothing else; the
+	 * forced VDD stays, as it does in libgfxinit until the panel is up.
+	 */
+	Method (PNON, 0, Serialized)
+	{
+		Local0 = GMMB ()
+		If (Local0 == 0) {
+			Return ()
+		}
+		OperationRegion (GFPP, SystemMemory, Local0 + 0xc7204, 4)
+		Field (GFPP, DWordAcc, NoLock, Preserve)
+		{
+			PPCT, 32,
+		}
+		Local1 = PPCT
+		If ((Local1 & 0xf) != 0x8) {
+			Return ()
+		}
+		PPCT = Local1 | 0x7
+	}
+}
diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/platform.asl b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/platform.asl
index bed1217185..90b175b00e 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/platform.asl
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/platform.asl
@@ -19,6 +19,17 @@ Method(_WAK,1)
 		\_SB.PCI0.GFX0.XBCM (\_SB.PCI0.GFX0.BRLV)
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * With the display left to the OS at wake (gfx_resume_init off), the
+	 * resume path gives the panel only VDD, for its HPD. macOS drives the
+	 * panel of the W541, on DDI D, as a DisplayPort sink: it trains the
+	 * link and runs the pipe, but never powers the panel up through the
+	 * sequencer nor enables the backlight. Do it here, after the level.
+	 */
+	If (Arg0 == 3 && \ISDW ()) {
+		\_SB.PCI0.GFX0.PNON ()
+	}
+
 	Return(Package(){0,0})
 }
 
diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/dsdt.asl b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/dsdt.asl
index d959faad0c..45249840bc 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/dsdt.asl
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/dsdt.asl
@@ -73,6 +73,8 @@ DefinitionBlock(
 		Scope (SBUS) { Name (_S3D, 3) }
 		Scope (RP03.PXSX) { Method (_RMV) { Return (1) } }
 		Scope (RP05.PXSX) { Method (_RMV) { Return (1) } }
+
+		#include "acpi/panel.asl"
 	}
 
 #if CONFIG(LENOVO_HASWELL_DGPU_RUNTIME_PM)
